WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.230
Who lives the longest and why?

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:09.750
Let’s take a look at the top 10 countries
with the healthiest citizens, based on a variety

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:17.240
of factors and find out exactly what they’re
doing right.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.100
10.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:29.880
First up with a life expectancy of 81.5 years
is the Netherlands.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:34.120
The Netherlands is widely regarded to offer
one of the highest standards of living in

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.239
the world.

00:00:35.239 --> 00:00:41.440
This is largely due to the countries’ relatively
low food prices and a diet that places emphasis

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.499
on vegetables, fruit and dairy products.

00:00:44.499 --> 00:00:51.219
A popular and highly nutritious meal in the
Netherlands is a Dutch Pea Soup called Snert,

00:00:51.219 --> 00:00:53.050
stuffed full of vegetables.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:54.050
9.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.820
At 9 is Canada.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:01.890
Amazingly Canada has one of the lowest number
of doctors per capita of any country in this

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:02.890
video.

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:06.490
With only 2.1 doctors for every 1,000 citizens.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:13.170
Yet Canadians enjoy one of the highest life
expectancies in the world at an average of

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.259
82.5 years.

00:01:14.259 --> 00:01:15.259
8.

00:01:15.259 --> 00:01:19.340
At 8 is Australia, with a life expectancy
of 83.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:23.320
Australians have one of the best health care
systems in the world.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:30.229
Down under, insurance companies are required
to charge policyholders the exact same premium,

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:33.350
regardless of their age, gender or history.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:39.829
Meaning no matter who you are or what you’ve
done you will pay the same as everyone else

00:01:39.829 --> 00:01:41.380
for your health insurance.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:42.380
7.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:47.119
At 7 is Switzerland, the Swiss have a life
expectancy of 82.8.

00:01:47.119 --> 00:01:53.050
The Swiss healthcare system has been named
the best in the world on many occasions.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:59.009
Naturally this helps, but the Swiss are also
lucky enough to be nestled right in the heart

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:05.090
of the Alps which means sports such as hiking
and skiing are prevalent, helping to keep

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:08.750
the Swiss people fit and healthy all year
round.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:09.750
6.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.909
At 6 is Germany.

00:02:11.909 --> 00:02:14.540
Germans pay handsomely for their healthcare.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:19.790
11.3% of the country’s GDP is spent on healthcare.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:25.110
There is no waiting for appointments in Germany
and until very recently you didn’t even

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:28.450
have to pay for your taxi ride to the hospital.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:29.450
5.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.239
At 5 is Finland.

00:02:31.239 --> 00:02:37.630
This may come as a surprise, because 35 years
ago Finland was one of the world’s unhealthiest

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:38.630
nations.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:44.150
And the country actually held the global record
for the highest numbers of heart disease.

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:47.340
But this shocked the Finnish Government into
action.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:52.840
The Government launched a full blown campaign
to dramatically improve people’s health

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:57.340
by encouraging an active lifestyle and promoting
fruit and vegetable intake.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:03.080
And it worked, present day Finland is a very
different place and rates of cardiovascular

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:06.519
heart disease have since dropped by over 65%.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.519
4.

00:03:07.519 --> 00:03:09.830
at 4 is Sweden.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:13.620
Sweden can owe most of it’s success to an
emphasis on staying active.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:18.599
The Swedish government invests a lot of money
in building new cycle routes and encouraging

00:03:18.599 --> 00:03:22.580
people to get out of their cars and cycle
instead.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:28.120
Some Swedish GPs even give patients “exercise
on prescription”.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:31.850
Sweden also has one of the lowest air pollution
rates in the world.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:32.850
3.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.370
At 3 is Iceland.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:39.150
With all the countries beautiful mountains,
glaciers, volcanoes, and waterfalls it’s

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:44.240
no surprise that the Icelandic love to spend
plenty of time enjoying the great outdoors.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:49.310
But the main reason Iceland is so high on
this list is because they eat practically

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:55.980
zero processed food, choosing to eat exclusively
locally grown food, even their organic food

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:01.829
is considerably less processed than in the
US and UK, Icelandic food is considered by

00:04:01.829 --> 00:04:05.239
many to be the purest on the planet.

00:04:05.239 --> 00:04:10.519
People don’t buy their produce from industrial
farms in Iceland, they instead buy from local

00:04:10.519 --> 00:04:12.000
family farms.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:17.060
The country has a strong lineage of hunting,
fishing and foraging, it’s what’s sustained

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:21.889
Iceland for centuries, and to a large extent
still does to this day.

00:04:21.889 --> 00:04:26.729
And to top it off Iceland is also one of the
least polluted countries in the world.

00:04:26.729 --> 00:04:27.729
2.

00:04:27.729 --> 00:04:28.850
At 2 is Japan.

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:33.789
Japan has been considered for many years to
be the world’s healthiest country.

00:04:33.789 --> 00:04:37.310
Obesity is virtually non-existent in the country.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:43.500
And they owe it to the Japanese tradition
of exercising strict portion control and eating

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.600
a wide variety of foods.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:51.229
The Japanese also choose the right foods to
eat, such as nutrient-rich soy and they are

00:04:51.229 --> 00:04:55.270
one of the world’s largest consumers of
omega-3 rich fish.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:05:01.370
A typical meal in Japan consists of up to
six teacup-sized portions of different foods,

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:03.310
and a lot of vegetables.

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:09.170
The Japanese aim to eat at 30-40 different
things every day, so they get a large variety

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:11.630
of nutrients and vitamins.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:16.600
Seaweed is also a major component in the Japanese
diet, highly regarded by the Japanese for

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:17.710
its health properties.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:23.380
Up to 6 varieties of seaweed are eaten every
day by the average Japanese citizen.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:26.910
The Japanese enjoy a life expectancy of 84.6.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:27.950
1.

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:32.160
At 1 is Okinawa Island.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:37.889
Okay it’s not actually a country, it’s
a small island belonging to Japan, south of

00:05:37.889 --> 00:05:39.770
the Japanese mainland.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:44.900
Okinawa Island has the highest percentage
of centenarians, that’s people over 100

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:47.780
years old, of anywhere in the world.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:51.920
It’s considered by many to be the healthiest
place in the world.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:56.670
They share the same healthy diet of fish,
rice and vegetables as the rest of Japan,

00:05:56.670 --> 00:06:02.449
but the Okinawans, have another ace up their
sleeves, they claim the biggest reason for

00:06:02.449 --> 00:06:06.509
their longevity is their happiness and lack
of stress.

00:06:06.509 --> 00:06:11.450
A lot of elderly in the West are struggling
to survive on small pensions with physical

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:16.600
pains and find the whole process of ageing
generally quite stressful.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:24.060
But not the Okinawans, they stay active even
at 100 plus and have a child-like zeal towards

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:32.009
life, stress just doesn’t seem to exist
on Okinawa Island.

